        "label": "Share a record by a sealed link",
        "job": "Share one record by a sealed link whose key rides only in the part after the #, so the store keeps only ciphertext it cannot read, and open it again from that link",
        "description": "op seal (the default): give id (the record id the copy is sealed under), record ({ type, value }) and address (the web address the link opens). The record is sealed with AES-GCM under a fresh 32-byte key of the link's own, the id bound as associated data; answers link (address with the key and the record id in its fragment, which a browser never sends to a server), sealed_copy ({ content_id, value }: the only thing to give the store, which cannot read it), content_id and opens (the copy opened again from the link in this run). op open: give id, link and copy (a sealed_copy); the copy is checked whole (one bounded sealed value matching its content_id) and opened with the key the link carries; answers record. Refuses, in plain words, another key, a changed or moved copy, a link with no key. It keeps and sends nothing; sealing with a device's own key, syncing ciphertext and sealed files are the device copy's and are not run here.",
        "read_only": true,
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "id"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "op": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "seal",
                "open"
              ]
            },
            "id": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "record": {
